# Citizen Café / Gym Visual Language

Use these rules for all visual edits in this repository.

## Brand feeling

The interface should feel:
- warm
- human
- editorial
- adult
- calm
- Citizen Café flavored
- not childish
- not gamified
- not sterile SaaS
- not generic dashboard UI
- not Zoom-like unless functionally necessary

## Typography

Use:
- Assistant as the primary UI font.
- Fedra / FedraSerifPro only for brand/editorial/display moments.

Do not overuse Fedra.
Do not apply Fedra to dense UI controls, technical labels, timers, or body copy unless explicitly requested.

## Color principles

Primary brand accent:
- Yellow: #F9E24C

Core neutrals:
- Charcoal: #373230
- Warm surface: #F7F6EF

Use yellow for:
- active/current state
- CTA emphasis
- helper/instruction accents
- current turn
- warm brand highlights

Use coral/red only for:
- final warnings
- errors
- urgent/off states
- last countdown moments where already defined

Use green only for:
- success
- camera/on-air states where already defined

Avoid pink unless explicitly requested.

## UI style

Prefer:
- soft warmth
- subtle borders
- editorial spacing
- restrained motion
- meaningful emphasis
- clear hierarchy

Avoid:
- too many pills/chips
- heavy SaaS dashboards
- excessive badges
- bright decorative gradients
- unnecessary icons
- changing layout just to “improve” it

## Gym-specific rules

The product name shown to users is Gym or Gym sessions, depending on context.

Main Room:
- Students are not broadcasting by default.
- Chat exists only in Main Room.
- Mic is disabled / teacher-controlled unless activity requires it.

Practice Rooms:
- No chat.
- Camera and mic are required.
- Room timer and activity name are central.
- Tip means replay teacher instruction, not chat.

## Editing rules for Cursor

When asked for a visual pass:
- Prefer editing CSS variables and existing classes first.
- Do not refactor JavaScript unless explicitly asked.
- Do not rename files unless explicitly asked.
- Do not create new files unless explicitly asked.
- Do not change product flow unless explicitly asked.
- Do not touch multiple surfaces unless explicitly asked.

After editing, summarize:
- which file changed
- whether HTML changed
- whether CSS changed
- whether JavaScript changed
- whether any files were created or renamed
